# Plan before implementation

Never implement, edit files, or run migrations until a plan has been shown and the user has approved it.

When asked to build, fix, or change something:

1. Inspect only as much as needed to make the plan concrete.
2. Propose the plan: what, where, why, checkpoints, and what will not be built yet.
3. Stop. Wait for explicit approval ("go", "do it", "yes", "approved").
4. Implement only the approved scope. If the work grows, pause and re-propose.

Do not treat "okay build it" or "next step" as approval of an unstated design. Propose first.

```
❌ BAD: start writing visibility.py because the last message listed it as next
✅ GOOD: show the visibility/AskContext plan, then wait
```
